Collision Handling in Hashing
When two different keys generate the same hash index, it is called a collision.
(Agar do different keys ka same index generate hota hai, to usse collision kehte hain.)

Techniques to Handle Collision:
Chaining (Separate Chaining)

Uses a LinkedList to store multiple values at the same index.
(Same index par multiple values ko LinkedList me store karta hai.)
Example: HashMap uses this method in Java.
Open Addressing (Linear Probing, Quadratic Probing, Double Hashing)

Instead of using a list, it finds the next available slot in the hash table.
(Agar index occupied ho, to next available slot dhundta hai.)
Types of Hashing
1. Static Hashing
Hash table size is fixed.
(Table ka size fix hota hai, naye data ke liye resize nahi hota.)
Example: Simple array-based hash table
2. Dynamic Hashing
Hash table grows or shrinks when needed.
(Agar data zyada ho jaye, to table ka size badhta hai.)
Example: Extendible Hashing used in databases.
Time Complexity of Hashing Operations
Operation	Average Case	Worst Case (Collision)
Insertion	O(1)	O(n) (Chaining)
Deletion	O(1)	O(n) (Chaining)
Searching	O(1)	O(n) (Chaining)
Real-Life Applications of Hashing
✅ Databases – Indexing for fast data retrieval
✅ Cache Systems – Quick access to frequently used data
✅ Cryptography – Password hashing for security
✅ Networking – Storing IP addresses in hash tables

When to Use Hashing?
✅ Jab aapko fast searching aur fast insertion chahiye.
✅ Jab duplicate values allow nahi karni ho (like in HashSet).
✅ Jab large datasets handle karne ho.

When NOT to Use Hashing?
❌ Jab sorting ya ordering maintain karni ho, hashing use nahi karna chahiye.
❌ Jab continuous memory allocation chahiye, kyunki hashing me memory scattered hoti hai.

Conclusion
Hashing ek efficient technique hai jo fast searching, insertion aur deletion provide karta hai.
Hash function key ko index me convert karta hai, jisme data store hota hai.
Collision handling techniques important hoti hain (Chaining, Open Addressing).
Data structures like HashMap, HashSet hashing ka use karte hain.
